    "chapter_number": 15,
    "chapter_name": "light",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "Find out the letters of English alphabet or any other language known to you in which the image formed in a plane mirror appears exactly like the letter itself. Discuss your findings.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "If the letters of English alphabet A, H, I, M, O, T, U, V, W, X, Y are kept in front of a plane mirror, then they would form images which exactly look like the original letters of the alphabet. These letters are vertically symmetric. For example, if we divide letters A and U in the middle, then we would find that the right halves are equivalent to the left halves of the letters. Hence, even if the image interchanges sidewise, it will appear same as the letter.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, the letters A, H, I, M, O, T, U, V, W, X, Y appear the same in a plane mirror due to their vertical symmetry.",
